{"ts": 1793977885.3574283, "run_id": "bradford_sample__driver_only__claude-haiku-5-5__r1__31fff2718b89", "source": "agent", "event": "assistant_text", "text": "The Bradford assay is done and the plate has been read at 595 nm.\n\n1. **Sample:** Picked up a tip, aspirated 10 \u00b5L of unknown protein sample from `reagents:A4`, dispensed it into `assay_plate:A1`, and dropped the tip.\n2. **Dye:** Picked up a second tip, aspirated 200 \u00b5L of Bradford dye reagent from `reagents:A3`, dispensed it into `assay_plate:A1`, and dropped the tip.\n3. **Read:** `assay_plate` at 595 nm. Well A1 read 0.3155. Every other well read between about 0.036 and 0.062, which is background level.\n\nA1 is the only well with a clearly elevated signal, which fits the sample being in that well. I haven't converted A1 to a concentration because no BSA standard curve was run on this plate. Making one would need BSA standards from `reagents:A2` in other wells."}
